(a) There shall be a written agenda prepared by the mayor prior to each meeting of the mayor and council. All regular council meetings shall follow an established order of business as follows:
(1) Call to order;
(2) Executive session (if needed);
(3) Consideration of minutes;
(4) Proclamations, recognitions, acknowledgements, presentations;
(5) Old business;
(6) New business;
(7) Announcements;
(8) Adjournment.
The Mayor and Council of Cumming may amend, add to and/or delete from an agenda or this established order of business for its meetings in conformance with Georgia law. Persons who desire to have an item included on the agenda for a meeting are required to notify the city clerk in writing no later than noon of the day prior to the meeting of the mayor and council for the item to be considered by the mayor for inclusion on the agenda. The subject matter of the item shall be specified in the request.
(b) Notwithstanding the notice requirement for inclusion on the agenda as specified in subsection (a) of this section, any person attending a meeting of the mayor and council may be recognized to address the mayor and council by the presiding officer.
(c) The proceedings of the mayor and council shall be generally governed by Robert's Rules of Order, Newly Revised, so far as applicable and not inconsistent with the special rules of the mayor and council, the Charter and this Code.
(d) In the event that a public hearing is part of the agenda of the mayor and council, or in the event that a member of the public is invited to address the mayor and council on any topic, the public comment or address shall be limited to no more than two minutes for any individual and ten minutes total, unless otherwise specifically provided by law or ordinance.
(Code 1998, § 2-32; Ord. of 5-15-2012, § 2; Ord. of 7-17-2012, § 1; Ord. of 7-20-2012, § 1)

