(a) No licensee or employee or agent of a licensee, in connection with the sale or other disposition of alcoholic beverages for consumption on the premises, shall:
(1) Offer or deliver any free alcoholic beverage to any person or group of persons;
(2) Except as set forth below, sell, offer to sell, or deliver to any person or group of persons any alcoholic beverage at a price less than the price regularly charged for such alcoholic beverage during the same calendar week, except at private functions not opened to the public;
a. A licensee may offer specific categories of discounted price alcoholic beverages (i.e., selecting beer, wine, or distilled spirits) subject to the following requirements:
1. The category of alcoholic beverages and the discount applied to such beverage shall be prominently displayed at the licensee's establishment such that enforcement personnel can identify what category of beverage is being discounted, the discount provided, and if applicable, the specific day (a "discount day") and time;
2. The licensee shall be entitled to limit a discount to a particular brand of alcoholic beverage within a specific category of beverage;
3. The licensee shall be entitled to limit a discount to a particular time of day in a similar manner as a "happy hour" or other time-specific special;
4. Licensees shall be authorized to offer and advertise regularly occurring discount days so long as all other requirements of this subsection receive compliance;
5. This subsection shall not authorize any increase in the volume of alcoholic beverage contained in a drink without proportionately increasing the price customarily charged for such beverage;
(3) Increase the volume of alcohol contained in a drink without increasing proportionately the price regularly charged for such alcoholic beverage during the same calendar week; or
(4) Encourage or permit on the licensed premises any game or contest which involves the drinking of alcoholic beverages or the awarding of alcoholic beverages as a prize.
(b) Each licensee shall maintain a schedule of the price charged for all alcoholic beverages to be served and consumed on the licensed premises. The licensee shall not vary the schedule of prices from day to day except as expressly authorized by this chapter. The schedule of prices shall be posted in a conspicuous manner so as to be in view of the paying public.
(c) No licensee shall advertise or promote in any way, whether within or without the licensed premises, any of the practices prohibited under subsection (a) of this section.
(d) No provision of this section shall be construed to prohibit licensees from offering free food or entertainment at any time, to prohibit licensees from including an alcoholic beverage as part of a meal package, or to prohibit the sale or delivery of wine by the bottle or carafe when sold with meals or to more than one person.
(e) The city police department shall have responsibility for the enforcement of this article.
(f) No licensee may require the purchase of any alcoholic beverage as a part of or as a prerequisite to the purchase of any other product or service. If alcoholic beverages are included as part of a package of other goods and/or services, the alcoholic beverages must be priced separately and all customers must be allowed to purchase the remaining goods and services without the alcoholic beverages at a price from which the full price of the alcoholic beverages has been deducted.
(g) Nothing contained in this section shall be interpreted to prohibit an on-premises consumption licensee from conducting a wine or malt beverage tasting which conforms to state law and any local ordinance provisions governing the same.
(Ord. of 3-19-2013(1), § 40; Ord. of 11-19-2024, § 1)
